+### Running Tests Locally
+
+When developing locally, especially in Docker or Trae environments, you might want to run tests for a specific package (e.g., a single controller) rather than the entire suite. To do this stably without invoking the full CI test suite, you can use the minimal runnable test command directly with `go test`.
+
+First, ensure the integration test dependencies (`etcd`, `kube-apiserver`, `kubectl`) are downloaded:
+```bash
+make _bin/tools/etcd _bin/tools/kube-apiserver _bin/tools/kubectl
+```
+
+Then, set the `KUBEBUILDER_ASSETS` environment variable to the downloaded tools directory and run `go test` for your desired package. For example, to test the ACME CertificateRequest controller:
+```bash
+export KUBEBUILDER_ASSETS="$(pwd)/_bin/tools"
+go test -v ./pkg/controller/certificaterequests/acme/...
+```
+
